\par
Appendix G \par
\par
\pard Tape Control Characters \par
\par
\pard\sl368\slmult0 Whenever TINY generates the \fs21 ? \fs22 prompt character (during execution of an INPUT statement), it follows this by generating the XON (ASCII DC1) control character. If the input comes from tape, the user may elect to use this special control character to activate the tape reader. \par
\par
Similarly, TINY generates the XOFF (ASCII DC3; hex 13; Control S) control character whenever an error stop or NEW or END occurs - under the assumption that the user may want to deactivate the reader with this character. \par
\par
\pard\sl366\slmult0 These control characters may \f1\fs18 be \f0\fs22 ignored if the user has found an alternative method for tape I/O. \par
\par
